    {
      "reading": "Each frame's own sampling frequency",
      "clause": "ETSI TS 102 114 V1.6.1 clause 5.4.2: every frame header codes SFREQ, the core sampling frequency of that frame (Table 5-5), and NBLKS, its window of 32 x (NBLKS + 1) samples",
      "candidate": "reports the second frame's own 44100 Hz and 512 samples",
      "reference": "the dca parser keeps the first frame's 48000 Hz and rescales the second frame's duration to 557 samples",
      "compat": "a consumer that needs one stream-wide rate, as the reference publishes, would use a compat::dts policy that latches the first frame's rate (not built)",
